    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d518-a1">

                <pb facs="1979" n="1874" xml:id="pg1874"/>


                <head>Covering Letter From Head to Merchant</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-01-15">January 15,
                        1960</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d518-2" n="2" type="facsimile" xml:id="d518-2"/>
                <p>My dear Livie</p>
                <p>I have received the enclosed message for Mr. Herter from Mr. Lloyd in reply to Mr. Dillon’s letter of January
                    6 about the Nuclear Tests Conference.</p>
                <p>As I know that the Secretary is still away I am sending the message to you so
                    that you can give it preliminary consideration in anticipation of his
                    return,</p>
                <p>Yours [illegible in the original]</p>
                <p>[illegible in the original]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Sammy</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">(Hood)</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
